WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.384 --> 00:00:03.776
- Diane, it's 9:15 a.m.

00:00:03.776 --> 00:00:05.300
The donuts are fresh and the sun shining

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:07.447
which means, as locals
like to say around here,

00:00:07.447 --> 00:00:10.910
“I’m as happy as a clam at
high-water on a Sunday.”

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:12.434
This morning, I woke up to a curious note

00:00:12.434 --> 00:00:14.125
under my bedroom door.

00:00:14.125 --> 00:00:17.805
It read, “The fat man who tore
down the wall wants to know…”

00:00:17.805 --> 00:00:19.630
Wants to know what?

00:00:19.630 --> 00:00:21.602
And who is the fat man?

00:00:21.602 --> 00:00:23.102
Let's investigate.

00:00:25.777 --> 00:00:28.840
Diane, we're once again
struck by the realization that

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:30.118
all of us on this planet Earth

00:00:30.118 --> 00:00:33.544
only understand a fraction
of what's going on around us.

00:00:33.544 --> 00:00:35.977
That's why I'm employing a
unique investigative strategy

00:00:35.977 --> 00:00:39.449
that relies both on ancient
Tibetan practices and intuition.

00:00:39.449 --> 00:00:41.879
Chance will be our guide.

00:00:41.879 --> 00:00:45.142
I'll read the name and
then I'll throw the rock.

00:00:45.142 --> 00:00:47.082
Mark Frost, TV writer.

00:00:47.082 --> 00:00:48.115
Miss.

00:00:48.115 --> 00:00:50.600
David Lynch, director.

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:51.508
Ugh.

00:00:51.508 --> 00:00:53.531
Brad Dukes, author.

00:00:53.531 --> 00:00:58.319
(whoosh)
(glass breaking)

00:00:58.319 --> 00:01:00.791
Let's call up Brad Dukes
who wrote this book,

00:01:00.791 --> 00:01:05.066
Reflections, An Oral
History of Twin Peaks.

00:01:05.066 --> 00:01:07.088
Operator, get me Brad Dukes.

00:01:07.088 --> 00:01:08.921
Brad, can you hear me?

00:01:10.516 --> 00:01:11.748
No time for pleasantries, Brad.

00:01:11.748 --> 00:01:13.037
I received a note under my door.

00:01:13.037 --> 00:01:16.338
It read The fat man who tore
down the wall wants to know...

00:01:16.338 --> 00:01:18.505
What does he want to know?

00:01:19.468 --> 00:01:23.621
It was Bob's spirit in
Millen's body, we know.

00:01:23.621 --> 00:01:27.204
The fat man wants to
know who killed Laura?

00:01:29.765 --> 00:01:30.848
Thanks, Brad.

00:01:35.372 --> 00:01:38.174
Operator, give me Jules
Haimovitz, TV exec.

00:01:38.174 --> 00:01:39.373
Jules, I received a note this morning

00:01:39.373 --> 00:01:41.609
whose contents you might
have the key to deciphering.

00:01:41.609 --> 00:01:44.451
It read, “The fat man who tore
down the wall wants to know…”

00:01:44.451 --> 00:01:47.534
I believe it's in reference to Laura.

00:01:48.665 --> 00:01:49.748
V. Gorbachev?

00:01:51.968 --> 00:01:54.113
Aaron Spelling, the TV exec.

00:01:54.113 --> 00:01:57.030
(mysterious music)

00:02:16.484 --> 00:02:19.620
Gorbachev, the eighth and final
leader of the Soviet Union?

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:21.703
What did he want to know?

00:02:26.595 --> 00:02:27.463
Thanks, Jules.

00:02:27.463 --> 00:02:28.296
Actually by now,

00:02:28.296 --> 00:02:32.463
the fat man who tore down
the wall knows the answer.

